## Preflight for OpenSpec work

When creating or implementing an OpenSpec change, check whether the change introduces a
[formal trigger](docs/ARCHITECTURE_REASSESSMENT.md#formal-triggers), especially:

- ownership transfer for mutable state;
- state transition changes;
- new top-level abstractions, Managers, or parallel authorities;
- behavior that conflicts with archived specs or architecture docs.

If no formal trigger fired, use lightweight preflight: short inline owner/change/test summary
before implementation.

If a formal trigger fired, complete a full preflight before firmware edits:

- use `docs/Templates/PREFLIGHT.md`;
- include ownership-transfer fields when mutable ownership moves;
- include `docs/Templates/DECISION_REVIEW.md` or equivalent findings;
- create a repo artifact such as `openspec/changes/<name>/PREFLIGHT.md` when the OpenSpec
  itself carries the design/implementation handoff;
- add explicit `tasks.md` items for preflight, decision log entry, compatibility removal trigger,
  and validation gates.

